  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "This study maps the cybersecurity landscape of smart ports by combining a systematic literature review following the PRISMA protocol, a bibliometric visualization using CiteSpace, and an empirical analysis of real-world cyberattack data. It identifies how technologies like IoT, AI, and blockchain expand attack surfaces and details vulnerabilities across cyber-physical systems, governance frameworks, and human factors.",
      "why": "It connects fragmented research on port digitalization directly to empirical cyberattack patterns, establishing a systematic framework for researchers and port authorities to design resilient, socio-technical maritime governance strategies."
